course: dictionary
lesson: 9898
title: Tale: a story, a tall tale, or tell tales
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tale is a story, often a made-up one with adventures in it. Read this: «Stories grow because people fill gaps with guesses, round numbers up, and add a twist that makes the tale better to tell.» Here tale means a story that people tell, so the words around it show you what it means.
explain: Look at the word before tale. Fairy tale, folk tale and tall tale are phrases, and the first word tells you what kind of story it is. «Some tales are nearly true, like the owl that turns its head "all the way round"; it turns about three-quarters of the way, and that is amazing enough.» This is a tale that sounds hard to believe at first, but it is still a story about a real animal.
explain: Tell tales is different, and it is not about stories at all. Check the sentence: if you swap in «a story», does it still make sense? If not, think about the whole phrase. It means telling someone in charge about another person's small mistakes.
fact: A tale is a story, often made up, with adventures in it.
fact: A fairy tale is a story with magic in it, and many fairy tales begin «Once upon a time».
fact: A folk tale and a fable are kinds of stories, and they are often old.
fact: A tall tale is a story that is hard to believe.
fact: To tell tales means telling someone in charge about another person's small mistakes.
exercise: «Stories grow because people fill gaps with guesses, round numbers up, and add a twist that makes the tale better to tell.» What does tale mean here? | A person in charge | A tall tree | *A story | A sweet, sticky treat
exercise: «Ukraine has a few thousand wolves, which hunt deer and boar and usually avoid people; in the folk tale Sirko an old dog and a wolf become friends.» Which kind of tale is Sirko? | Telling tales | A fairy tale | *A folk tale | A tall tale
exercise: Joe says, «Don't tell tales on me, I only dropped my pencil.» What does tell tales mean? | *Tell someone in charge about another person's small mistake | Tell a joke that makes everyone laugh | Tell a story that is hard to believe | Tell a fairy story with magic in it
test: Which kind of tale has magic in it? | *A fairy tale | To tell tales | A tall tale
test: Which phrase means a story that is hard to believe? | Folk tale | *Tall tale | Fairy tale | Tell tales
exam: Which phrase means telling someone in charge about another person's small mistakes? | *Tell tales | Tall tale | Folk tale | Fairy tale
